# Task 12 measurement checkouts (large upstream clones, never committed)
.packwork/

# Built packs (large artifacts, published out of band)
dist/

# Built knowledge packs. Hundreds of MB of binary SQLite, rebuildable from
# the pinned upstream checkouts -- an artifact, not source. A `git add -A`
# swept 1.19 GB of these into a commit and the push died on it.
#
# Leading slash matters: a bare `packs/` matches any directory of that name at
# any depth, which silently excluded argus/packs/ and tests/packs/ -- the pack
# source tree itself. Already-tracked files kept working, so the only symptom
# was new files there refusing to be added.
/packs/
